   :entries [["ai-gftd-cyber-drill" "83 KB, archived, last pushed 2026-07-29"]
             ["ai-gftd-kotoba" "1 KB, archived, last pushed 2026-06-30"]]
   :preserved "Mirror bundles under ~/repo-archive/, one per repository, each verified with `git bundle verify` before anything was deleted. All six repositories touched in this wave were bundled first, not only the two that were deleted, because a transfer is only reversible while you still know what was in it."}
  :kotobase-resolved
  {:landed "GitHub transfer + rename, west.yml a9ea7fac, pin 62320779"
   :what "cloud-itonami/kotobase -> net-kotobase/control-plane-retired. Owner chose 移動 over 削除."
   :why-that-name "Reading it settled the question. It is a TOMBSTONE: seven files, of which MOVED.md.edn says '[MOVED] kotobase -> net-kotobase ... This leftover CF Worker (superseded control plane) has been extracted to net-kotobase (worker/)'. Its successor is net-kotobase/control-plane, 49.9 MB, so the remnant is control-plane-retired and it belongs beside what replaced it. The net-kotobase org names everything bare (control-plane, ipfs, sdk, docs, engine, authn) because the org carries the identity; this follows that."
   :collision-gone "The west name kotobase stays with kotoba-lang/kotobase, whose gate and repo-bots entries are untouched."
